      "info": {
        "description": "Fast IP lookups to get information about open ports",
        "servers": [
          {
            "url": "https://internetdb.shodan.io"
          }
        ],
        "title": "InternetDB",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "Fast IP lookups for open ports, hostnames, CPEs, tags, and known CVEs",
        "homepage": "https://internetdb.shodan.io",
        "docs_url": "https://internetdb.shodan.io",
        "license_short": "Free for non-commercial use; commercial use requires Shodan enterprise licensing",
        "license_md": "- Free to use for non-commercial purposes with no API key or account required\n- Commercial use requires enterprise licensing from Shodan\n- Data is provided as-is and reflects Shodan's most recent scan cycle\n- See the [Shodan terms of service](https://www.shodan.io/) for the full agreement",
        "about_md": "[InternetDB](https://internetdb.shodan.io) is a free, lightweight lookup service from [Shodan](https://www.shodan.io/) that returns a summary view of what Shodan knows about a public IPv4 address. It is intended for quick reconnaissance rather than the deep banner-level data offered by the full Shodan API.\n\nWhat you get from the API:\n\n- The queried IP address\n- The list of open `ports`\n- `cpes` (Common Platform Enumerations) detected on the host\n- Associated `hostnames`\n- `tags` describing the host (for example `vpn`, `cloud`)\n- Known `vulns` as CVE identifiers\n\nThe service is unauthenticated and CORS-enabled, making it convenient to call directly from browsers, scripts, or CLI tools. Data is refreshed on a weekly cadence rather than in real time, and no banner content is included. Only public IPv4 addresses that Shodan has observed will return data; unknown addresses produce a 404.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "info_ip_get": "Per-IP reconnaissance record returned by `GET /{ip}` — the open ports, CPEs, hostnames, tags, and known CVE IDs Shodan has observed for that address."
        },
